\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {29}{\ignorespaces The ``creep up'' trajectory showing three phases of the two-step detection process. Phase~1: fast flight with tilted camera produces a rough GPS estimate (large error ellipse). Phase~2: the drone decelerates toward the estimate, pitch decreases, and accuracy improves (medium error ellipse). Phase~3: the drone hovers directly above the target with the camera at nadir, producing the precise lock (small error ellipse). Camera cones show the field of view at each phase; the blue triangles represent the drone oriented in its direction of travel.}}{76}{figure.caption.177}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:creep-up}{{29}{76}{The ``creep up'' trajectory showing three phases of the two-step detection process. Phase~1: fast flight with tilted camera produces a rough GPS estimate (large error ellipse). Phase~2: the drone decelerates toward the estimate, pitch decreases, and accuracy improves (medium error ellipse). Phase~3: the drone hovers directly above the target with the camera at nadir, producing the precise lock (small error ellipse). Camera cones show the field of view at each phase; the blue triangles represent the drone oriented in its direction of travel}{figure.caption.177}{}}
